# The RPC header-propagation fixture's per-loop body bounds (K_L).
#
# Schema: {"loopSiteId": "<signature>#u<unitIndex>", "loopBodyBound": K_L,
#          "reason": "..."} -- one row per retained condition-controlled loop,
# exactly as in experiments/hdfs/hdfs-11741/loop-bounds.jsonl.
#
# This file declares no row, and that is the statement it exists to make.  The
# fixture's failure-relevant chain is two RPC producer helpers and one
# NameNode-side comparison; it retains no while loop and no other
# data-dependent loop, so there is no K_L for this workload to state.  The
# array-backed reads it does perform are fixed-count within one invocation and
# carry their exact N in the occurrence plan, which is not this file's business
# (README section "Loops").
#
# The file is here rather than absent because run_engine.sh requires
# causynth_loop_bounds of every workflow: an absent key and a campaign whose
# declarations never arrived look identical at runtime, and both would leave
# every retained loop quietly inheriting the core default.  "None" is a claim
# a reader can check against the plan.  If a future scenario adds a retained
# condition loop, its row belongs here -- an empty file is then wrong in a way
# the plan's loop rows will show.
